 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Draw lightly with fast pencil lines, and don't shade until the end. People tend to over shade and make things look flat. Of course not. A face can be drawn in ten. Draw the lines lightly and keep the eyes and mouth simple. Find a drawn reference you like, and use the shadow line under it to copy it. Then do the same with picture of yourself, drawing only the eyes. That's okay, it' a common feeling. Just keep practising and don't stop at the first drawing you don't like.",
